						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=912.msg10521#msg10521"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=912.msg10521#msg10521">Re: (No topic kinda pointless yet redundant topic)</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #23 on:</b> August 27, 2004, 08:05:04 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							To me the CRTC is there to protect Canadian interests...&nbsp; You&#039;d be suprised at the talent we have but often gets squashed because of big American Network shows.&nbsp; (Check out a show called Corner Gas it&#039;s FUNNY).<br /><br />We have the Fox channel, it&#039;s the American one tho.&nbsp; American news, shows, etc.&nbsp; We get the news from Washington State here...&nbsp; Back home we get news from New York and Burlington.&nbsp; I think if they were to open up a Fox Canada news channel it would take away from the news shows that are all ready there.&nbsp; But what do I know...&nbsp; As far as Al-Jabooboo...&nbsp; I dunno.<br /><br /> <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/banghead2.gif" alt="banghead2" border="0" />
						</td>
					</tr>
